-- The real club_directory dataset (1385 of 1389 extracted clubs), generated
-- from scripts/ingestion/out/club_directory_staging.csv -- the same staged
-- output the remote-only scripts/ingestion/import_club_directory.sql
-- consumes, just re-shaped as plain INSERT statements instead of a
-- server-side \copy so it runs identically regardless of how the CLI's
-- `sql_paths` seeding executes a file. Runs after seed.sql (see
-- supabase/config.toml [db.seed] sql_paths) on every `db reset --local`.
--
-- Added because local dev club search previously ran against only 5
-- hand-written sample clubs (seed.sql's own block below this one), so any
-- real club outside that tiny list -- Clitheroe, Didsbury Toc H, or any of
-- the other 1387 -- was correctly unfindable: not a search bug, a local
-- data gap. This is the same real, sourced data that was already
-- successfully extracted for the remote import; loading it locally too
-- doesn't touch remote and isn't fabricated data.
--
-- Deliberately EXCLUDES 4 of the 1389 staged rows that collide with the 5
-- hand-written local_dev_seed fixture clubs below (seed.sql runs first):
-- club_directory.name has no uniqueness constraint, so loading both
-- unfiltered produced real duplicate rows for the same real-world club
-- under two names/sources -- e.g. "Burnley RUFC" (local_dev_seed) next to
-- "Burnley RUFC" (official_club, same town/postcode) -- caught live via
-- signup search showing Burnley and Blackburn twice. Each exclusion below
-- was verified individually against town/county/postcode context, not a
-- blind fuzzy match, since a same-named club in a different place would be
-- a real, distinct club that must never be silently merged:
--   - Burnley RUFC (official_club) -- exact name + town(Burnley) +
--     county(Lancashire) match against the local_dev_seed fixture.
--   - Blackburn Rugby Union Football Club (charity_commission) -- same
--     town(Blackburn)/county(Lancashire) as the "Blackburn RUFC"
--     local_dev_seed fixture; "RUFC" vs the spelled-out formal name is a
--     naming-convention difference, not a different club.
--   - Preston Grasshoppers (wikipedia_candidate_population) -- name is a
--     direct substring of the "Preston Grasshoppers RFC" local_dev_seed
--     fixture; this candidate-population row carries no town/postcode of
--     its own to cross-check against, but the name itself is distinctive
--     enough that a coincidental unrelated match is implausible.
--   - Rossendale (wikipedia_candidate_population) -- same reasoning as
--     Preston Grasshoppers, against the "Rossendale RUFC" fixture.
-- The local_dev_seed rows are kept as the canonical local record for these
-- 4 clubs (not replaced) because existing local test/walkthrough fixtures
-- (supabase/tests/*.sql, the activated `clubs` rows) already reference
-- those specific club_directory ids by foreign key; swapping which row
-- "wins" would break those references for no benefit in a local dev seed.
--
-- To regenerate after a fresh extraction, re-run the generator that
-- produced this file against the current staging CSV (see git history for
-- the exact one-off script used), keeping the same exclusion list unless
-- the 5 local_dev_seed fixtures themselves change.
